<title>USA: Mexico buys 2,200 tonnes U.S. HRW wheat - trade.</title>
<headline>Mexico buys 2,200 tonnes U.S. HRW wheat - trade.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-03-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico Thursday night bought a small shipment of 2,200 tonnes of U.S. hard red winter wheat for early April arrival, several U.S. exporters said.</p>
<p>The wheat was bought at around $188 a tonne, cost and freight, via rail, basis Nogales, Ariz., one U.S. exporter said.</p>
<p>But Mexico was expected to retender for 8,000 to 28,000 tonnes of U.S. HRW wheat early next week, he said.</p>
<p>&quot;They are asking for prices every day,&quot; a second U.S. exporter said.</p>
<p>((Doris Frankel 312-983-7305))</p>
